Title: The September 11 Attacks: A Hoax?

\begin{frame}
\frametitle{Introduction}

The September 11 attacks in 2001 were a series of coordinated terrorist attacks carried out by the Islamic extremist group al-Qaeda against the United States. The attacks resulted in the deaths of nearly 3,000 people and caused significant damage to the World Trade Center in New York City, the Pentagon in Arlington, Virginia, and a plane crash in Pennsylvania.

However, there are some individuals and groups who believe that the September 11 attacks were a hoax. In this presentation, we will examine five steps to evaluate the validity of these claims.

